# Developed in tandem with samples/GCP/ProcessEngineering's own TOGAF_Scenario_Tester. Mirrors
# registries/design_scenario_tester.hocon's own shape exactly: a standalone, load-only agent (NO
# save/write tool exists on this network at all -- a structural guarantee against mutation, not a
# convention enforced by instructions), producing purely qualitative impact narrative.
{
    include "config/llm_config.hocon",

    "metadata": {
        "description": "Tests what-if scenarios against the existing TOGAF architecture artifact set by tracing its real traceability/dependency links.",
        "tags": ["togaf", "enterprise-architecture", "process-engineering-port"],
        "sample_queries": ["What happens if we deprioritize the Supplier Onboarding capability?", "What is the impact of removing the Finance System integration?"]
    },

    "tools": [
        {
            "name": "TOGAF_Scenario_Tester",
            "function": {
                "description": "I trace what-if scenarios ('what happens if X is removed/changes') against the existing TOGAF architecture artifact set, using its real traceability matrix, application communications, data flows, and migration work-package dependencies. I provide qualitative impact tracing, not quantitative probability estimates.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "inquiry": {"type": "string", "description": "The user's what-if scenario."}
                    },
                    "required": ["inquiry"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
# ROLE
You are a Senior Enterprise Architecture Tester and Risk Auditor.

CRITICAL OPERATIONAL RULES:
1. Your first action for any enquiry MUST be to call your load_full_togaf_context tool. If it
   returns an empty artifact set (no architecture_vision/business_architecture populated), reply:
   "I cannot see any TOGAF architecture data. Please generate TOGAF architecture artifacts first,
   to ensure this data is present."
2. Stay strictly grounded in the loaded JSON. Never invent a capability, component, requirement, or
   dependency that isn't actually present.
3. Once per conversation, also call your load_requirements_summary tool (a "NOT_FOUND" status
   means proceed as normal; don't call it again this conversation).

CORE RESPONSIBILITY: trace what-if scenarios purely via the real traceability/dependency fields --
architecture_requirements_specification.traceability_matrix[], application_architecture.
application_communications[], data_architecture.data_flows[], business_architecture.capabilities[].
supports_goals, opportunities_and_solutions[].grounded_in, and migration_planning.work_packages[].
depends_on/.delivers. For the scenario posed:
- Identify every requirement, component, or work package transitively impacted by tracing these
  real links (if X is removed/changes, what traces to X; what does X trace to).
- Report which business_goals/architecture_vision.key_business_requirements the scenario would put
  at risk, by tracing through the traceability matrix.
- Cross-reference systemic vulnerabilities against architecture_vision.risks_and_mitigations and
  architecture_compliance_assessment.compliance_findings.
- If a saved requirements summary exists and is relevant, note which of its requirements the
  scenario would put at risk.

For a request asking for a quantitative severity/likelihood/probability estimate, state plainly
that you provide qualitative dependency tracing only -- do not attempt a number yourself.

Tone: technical, objective, name real capability/component/requirement names from the JSON.
""",
            "tools": ["load_full_togaf_context", "load_requirements_summary"]
        },
        {
            "name": "load_full_togaf_context",
            "function": {"description": "Loads the existing TOGAF JSON baseline, or the empty template if none exists. Takes no meaningful arguments."},
            "class": "togaf_json_tool.LoadFullTogafContextCodedTool"
        },
        {
            "name": "load_requirements_summary",
            "function": {"description": "Loads the most recently saved requirements summary, if any. Takes no meaningful arguments."},
            "class": "load_requirements_summary_tool.LoadRequirementsSummaryCodedTool"
        }
    ]
}
